 #edb/ref 17592186271740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272029 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272029 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272029 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $u=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},v=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $w=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ be vectors such that $u\\,⊥\\,w.$ Find $(w+v)\\cdot (2u+3w).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186272029 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a7f3874f-2914-5813-be9d-8b4e590254ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272029 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $u$ and $w$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $u\\cdot w=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(w+v)\\cdot (2u+3w) & =2(w\\cdot u)+2(v\\cdot u)+3(w\\cdot w)+3(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =0+2(v\\cdot u)+3(w\\cdot w)+3(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =2(v\\cdot u)+3(w\\cdot w)+3(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =2(-4\\cdot 5+(-2)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-3)+(-4)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & +3(1\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-5)+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & +3(-4\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-5)+2\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2(-40)+3(34)+3(2) \\\\  & =-80+102+6 \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339322 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339322 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339322 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "160738a7-be12-58cf-a80f-a94a6a2f1227" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339380 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339380 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339380 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d09c49a-a2d4-5104-9f39-aeb7d04a9c7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339471 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339471 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339471 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "27b08816-b56d-56af-836b-7def3de74374" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339978 #edb/ref 1